sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant C as MCP Client
    participant O as OAuthProvider (/authorize, /callback)
    participant G as Google OAuth
    participant K as OAUTH_KV / TOKEN_KV

    C->>O: GET /authorize?client_id=&redirect_uri=&code_challenge=(S256)&state=
    O->>O: parseAuthRequest(req) + lookupClient / redirect_uri / PKCE S256 check
    O->>K: put oauthstate:<state> = AuthRequest
    alt (client_id, redirect_uri) not in signed approval cookie
        O-->>C: 200 approval page (client name, redirect host, all registered redirect_uris) + Set-Cookie state
        C->>O: POST /authorize (state, Cookie: state)
        O->>O: form state == state cookie (CSRF)
        O-->>C: 302 to Google + Set-Cookie approved (client_id, redirect_uri) keys (HMAC)
    else pair already approved in this browser
        O-->>C: 302 to Google + Set-Cookie state
    end
    C->>G: GET auth endpoint (scope=drive.file drive.readonly ...)
    G-->>C: consent screen
    C->>G: approve
    G-->>C: 302 to /callback?code=&state=
    C->>O: GET /callback?code=&state= (Cookie: state)
    O->>O: state cookie == state (browser binding)
    O->>K: get oauthstate:<state>
    K-->>O: AuthRequest
    O->>G: POST /token (code -> tokens)
    G-->>O: access_token, refresh_token, expires_in
    O->>G: GET /userinfo
    G-->>O: { sub, email }
    O->>K: put gtoken:<userId> (TOKEN_KV)
    O->>O: completeAuthorization({ userId, scope, props })
    O-->>C: 302 to client redirect_uri with code (clear state cookie)
    C->>O: POST /oauth/token (code + code_verifier)
    O-->>C: MCP access_token (bound to grant props)
